# Texts of many scripts and shapes, and the tokens tiktoken 0.14.0 makes of
# each with `encode_ordinary` in `o200k_base` and in `cl100k_base`, the
# expected values of `tokenizer/tables`' tests. Nothing here is edited by
# hand: a one-off program, `gen_texts.py`, kept outside the tree in the
# round's scratch folder (`.claude/worktrees/rebel-scratch/tokenizer/gen/`),
# wrote the 64 fragments it holds, then 140 seeded mixtures of them with
# white space between, asked tiktoken, and wrote this module whole on
# 2026-11-18. Scripts: Latin, Cyrillic, Greek, Armenian, Georgian, Hebrew,
# Arabic, Devanagari, Tamil, Thai, Ethiopic, Tibetan, Myanmar, Han, Kana,
# Hangul; emoji with modifiers and joiners, marks, digits of four scripts,
# every kind of white space, code, runs of one character.

# The texts.
constant TEXTS: [str]
    [
        "Hello, world!"
        "I'm here; you'LL see. It's they'Re, WE'VE, he'd, I'M"
        "don’t O'Neil's 'S 's"
        "def f(x):\n    return x**2  # square\n"
        "for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n\tsum += a[i];\n}"
